Package: ltsp6-session-tuning
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, x11-common
Recommends: xfwm4
Description: tuning for hosts running many desktop sessions at once
 Settings for an LTSP application server: a host where a lot of people are
 logged into graphical sessions simultaneously, over RDP, with or without a
 GPU for the sessions.
 .
 It moves each session's cache off the home directory onto local disk and
 keeps the browsers' share of it small. It turns off window manager
 compositing and vblank waiting by default. It raises the inotify limits a
 full Xfce session spends freely, limits dirty page cache to small absolute
 amounts so write-back does not stall sessions, and gives programs that keep
 secrets out of swap 64 MB of locked memory. It switches off the desktop
 search indexer and makes the screen saver blank and locking.
 .
 The settings are deliberately few. README.Debian lists what was left out
 after being measured as already correct on Debian 13, so the next person
 does not spend an afternoon re-adding it.
